    <!-- About -->

    <string name="about_title">Recipes %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_what">Recipes kept on this phone. It goes online to read a recipe page you send it, keeping the words and not the pictures, and to sync with your own Nextcloud if you sign in to one.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_head">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">Your recipes stay on this phone. The app collects nothing about you and has no ads or analytics. It goes online only to read a recipe page whose address you sent it (one page, no pictures or scripts, only over https, saying plainly that it is this app). Recipe text you paste or share here never leaves the phone and, once you sign in to your own Nextcloud, to sync your recipes with it. The Nextcloud app password is kept on the phone, sealed with a key that cannot leave it; you can revoke it from the server. Backups and exports go only where you choose to save them.</string>
    <string name="about_terms_head">Terms</string>
    <string name="about_terms">This app is free software under the GNU General Public License v3. It comes with no warranty: use it at your own risk. A recipe page is saved for your own use only; the recipe stays its writer\'s.</string>
